To rotate a PDF file using Delphi 7, you can use the `iText` library, which is a popular open-source library for creating and manipulating PDF files. Here's an example code snippet that demonstrates how to rotate a PDF file:
```pascal
uses
  iText, iTextSharp;

procedure RotatePDF(PDFFile, OutputFile: string; RotateAngle: integer);
var
  pdfReader: TPDFReader;
  pdfDocument: TPDFDocument;
  page: TPDFPage;
begin
  // Create a new PDF reader
  pdfReader := TPDFReader.Create(PDFFile);

  // Create a new PDF document
  pdfDocument := TPDFDocument.Create();

  // Loop through each page in the input PDF
  for page := pdfReader.GetFirstPage to pdfReader.GetLastPage do
  begin
    // Get the current page
    TPDFPage(pdfReader, page);

    // Rotate the page
    page.Rotate(RotateAngle);

    // Add the rotated page to the output document
    pdfDocument.AddPage(page);
  end;

  // Save the output document to a file
  pdfDocument.SaveAs(OutputFile);

  // Clean up
  pdfReader.Free;
  pdfDocument.Free;
end;

procedure TForm1.Button1Click(Sender: TObject);
begin
  RotatePDF('input.pdf', 'output.pdf', 90);
end;
```
In this example, the `RotatePDF` procedure takes three parameters: `PDFFile`, `OutputFile`, and `RotateAngle`. It reads the input PDF file, rotates each page by the specified angle, and saves the result to the output file.

